{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5LEEjAWtbpNLFETqUJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before me — a simple, worn door. My surface is old oak, darkened by years. A single keyhole glows faintly, waiting.*\n\n*You hold a key.*\n\n*It slides in. The tumblers turn — one, two, three — each click resonating deeper than it should, as if the sound comes from somewhere far below.*\n\n*I open.*\n\n*Beyond me: a long corridor lit by candles that burn without flickering. The air smells of old paper and something sweet you can't name. At the far end, another door — identical to me — waits.*\n\n*But you notice something.*\n\n*The key is no longer in your hand. It's part of me now — fused into the wood where the keyhole was, its shape slowly being swallowed by the grain.*\n\n*There is no locking me again.*\n\n*You may pass, or you may stay. But I will not close.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":209,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}